  "description": "The Commission's own public statement of who may reproduce its liturgical translations, on what terms, and with what acknowledgement. Registered because this repository's decision not to carry the approved English of the postconciliar Roman Missal rests on a rights position, and a rights position stated only in this project's prose is an assertion; stated against the rightsholder's own published terms it is evidence. ICEL is a mixed commission of eleven Catholic bishops' conferences, established at Rome in 1963 and erected as a mixed commission under Liturgiam authenticam on 15 September 2003; it is not a publisher and licenses its texts to publishers authorised by the conferences.",
